1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:05,352
Which e POS terminal does the processing center expect each debit to come through?

2
00:00:05,402 --> 00:00:11,880
It only accepts debits from e POS terminals it already knows: a MID and a TID it issued.

3
00:00:11,930 --> 00:00:19,368
So the e POS module keeps a registry: for each website and card scheme, one merchant ID and one terminal ID.

4
00:00:19,418 --> 00:00:24,648
Uzcard and Humo payments can use different e POS terminals for the very same website.

5
00:00:24,698 --> 00:00:31,488
An e POS terminal is registered only for a website that exists and accepts that card, and the check fails closed.

6
00:00:31,538 --> 00:00:40,104
The database allows one live e POS terminal per website and card, and a merchant and terminal ID pair is never issued twice.

7
00:00:40,154 --> 00:00:51,648
A Uzcard e POS terminal is also registered at Uzcard's SV-Gate, terminal add and then terminal check, and it is kept only if Uzcard accepts it, so a retry is always safe.

8
00:00:51,698 --> 00:00:59,904
Suspend and resume stay in our registry, because SV-Gate has no method to pause a terminal, and a revoked one never comes back.

9
00:00:59,954 --> 00:01:08,472
Revoking a Uzcard e POS terminal removes it from SV-Gate first, and if Uzcard refuses or stays silent, nothing changes.

10
00:01:08,522 --> 00:01:17,664
Admins check any Uzcard e POS terminal at SV-Gate, terminal check and terminal get side by side, and register one that SV-Gate never got.

11
00:01:17,714 --> 00:01:21,288
Every change is written to an audit log: who, what, and why.

12
00:01:21,338 --> 00:01:29,232
Before every debit, the payment module asks for the live e POS terminal, and no e POS terminal means no debit.

13
00:01:29,282 --> 00:01:37,224
The e POS module also lists a scheme's active and suspended terminals, so the card module can reconcile each one with Humo.

14
00:01:37,274 --> 00:01:47,664
Admins find any e POS terminal by website, card scheme, or status, or by part of its merchant or terminal ID, and open it to see its history and act on it.

15
00:01:47,714 --> 00:01:51,456
Next, the card schemes themselves: talking to Uzcard and Humo.
